        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(synology-chat): evict stale chat user cache entries",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the `chatUserCache` Map in Synology Chat could leak memory when callers rotated through many webhook URLs. The cache checked TTL only on reads; stale entries from old URLs were never removed from the Map, so a hostile or misconfigured caller cycling through webhook URLs could grow the Map without bound for the lifetime of the process.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis is a root-cause fix at the cache insertion boundary: before inserting a new entry, `fetchChatUsers` now evicts all stale entries. The change reuses the existing `CACHE_TTL_MS` constant and `cachedAt` timestamp already present on every cache entry. No config, schema, storage, or public API surface changes; the read path (freshness check before returning cached data) is unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSynology Chat channels that reference many webhook URLs no longer leak memory from stale cache entries. Existing single-URL and low-rotation deployments are unchanged — the eviction pass is an O(n) scan over entries that only fires on successful cache writes.\n\n## Evidence\n\nTDD reproduction before the production change:\n\n```\nFAIL |extension-messaging| extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts > fetchChatUsers > evicts stale cache entries when inserting a fresh one\nAssertionError: expected true to be false // Object.is equality\n\n- Expected\n+ Received\n\n- false\n+ true\n\n ❯ extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts:475:39\n    474|   // Verify stale urlA was evicted\n    475|   expect(chatUserCache.has(listUrlA)).toBe(false);\n       |                                       ^\n    476|\n    477|   // Verify fresh urlB is still present\n\n Test Files  1 failed (1)\n      Tests  1 failed | 22 passed (23)\n```\n\nAfter the fix — stale entry evicted on insert, fresh entry preserved:\n\n```\n ✓ |extension-messaging| extensions/synology-chat/src/client.test.ts > fetchChatUsers > evicts stale cache entries when inserting a fresh one 1ms\n\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  23 passed (23)\n```\n\nScoped checks:\n```\noxlint: pass\ngit diff --check: pass\n```\n\nImpact-surface review confirmed `fetchChatUsers` is the sole write path for `chatUserCache`; no other code mutates the Map. The eviction pass iterates entries and deletes any whose `cachedAt` is outside `CACHE_TTL_MS` — the same constant used by the read-path freshness check.",
        "branch": "fix/stdout-safety-wave-dir-fetch-browser",
